corbell5571@juno.com (Corbell5571) wrote:
> I am unclear on the concepts of bone piles and polypiles. I assume
> bone pile forms when a player character dies; but how does anyone FIND
> a bone pile? Isn't the dungeon individually generated for every new
> character?

If a character dies there is a certain chance that he leaves a bone pile
(the deeper into the dungeon he is, the higher is this chance). If you
enter a level for the first time and another character who died on this
very same level left a bones pile, there is a certain chance that the
game restores the level as it was when the character died rather than
creating a new one.

> What are polypiles?

Make a pile of useless items on the ground and zap a wand of polymorph
at it, pick up the items that polymorphed into something useful, repeat.

> Once you got the stuff out of a chest (or a box), is there any reason
> to lug it around? It seriously adds to my burden, and putting things
> into the chest does not seem to ease it.

The only reason would be if you want to carry the chest somewhere (for
example to your base camp, if you have one (useful to store items you
don't need right now, but might need later)). Other than that there is
no reason to pick up the chest at all (you can open and loot it while it
is on the ground)

